## Why This Is Asked
This question tests CGO callback safety, cross-language memory ownership, and streaming backpressure handling—critical skills for building high-performance Go/C interop layers.

## Key Concepts
- **CGO Trampolines & Go Handles**: Enable safe callbacks from C into Go without exporting Go pointers
- **Cross-Language Memory Ownership**: C malloc must be matched with C free (via C.free), not Go garbage collection
- **Thread Safety**: Callbacks from C may occur on arbitrary threads; synchronization is required
- **Backpressure**: Worker pools limit concurrent processing to prevent memory exhaustion during streaming

